.# .gitignore for handy-games-publisher
# This file lists paths that should not be committed to the repository.
#
# Organization:
#  - Environment / secrets
#  - Package manager / build outputs (Node, Rust, etc.)
#  - Generated build artefacts and runtime data
#  - CI / pipeline manifests (local copies)
#  - Tauri / platform-specific generated files
#  - Documentation build outputs
#
# Keep entries minimal and explain why each group is ignored.

# --- Environment / secrets ---
# Local environment variables and secret files used for local development.
.env

# --- Node / JavaScript artifacts ---
# Node modules and frontend build outputs are generated and should not be
# committed. `src-react/dist/` is the built web assets for the desktop UI.
node_modules/
src-react/node_modules/
src-react/dist/

# --- Temporary and data directories ---
# Transient files and runtime data produced on the developer machine.
data/
tmp/
.tmp*/

# --- Pipeline manifests (local edits) ---
# Local pipeline manifests used during development/testing. These are
# intentionally ignored to avoid accidental publishing of local or forked
# pipeline files.
pipelines/*.yml
pipelines/*.yaml

# --- Rust / Cargo build outputs ---
# Rust's `target/` directory contains compiled artifacts.
target/
/target-*/

# --- Tauri / desktop shell generated files ---
# Tauri generates code and binaries under `src-tauri/gen/` and `src-tauri/bin/`.
# We keep generated platform assets out of version control.
src-tauri/gen/
src-tauri/bin/

# --- Release artifacts ---
# Folder used to stage produced releases and installers. Kept local.
releases/

# --- Documentation site build output ---
# `site/` is the MkDocs generated site output. The source for documentation
# lives under `public-docs/` (public) and `developer-docs/` (internal).
# We build `site/` during CI or locally; do not commit it.
site/

# === Notes ===
# - If a file under these folders must be tracked for a specific reason
#   (e.g., an intentionally checked-in static asset), use an explicit
#   whitelist in `.git/info/exclude` or add a short project-specific note
#   and remove only that entry.
# - To stop tracking an already-tracked folder, run:
#     git rm -r --cached <path>
#   then commit the change.